  "details": "If you set a constraint target, activate, then deactivate (ie unchecking the Is Active) and set a new constraint target and activate again, it keeps the offsets already in the constraint instead of adjusting them, moving the object you just constrained relative to the world, instead of applying new offsets to keep it the same relative to world position. This is different behavior than default unity constraints.",
